{"cwe_mapping": "Based on the analysis provided, the most relevant Common Weakness Enumeration for the identified issue is:
CWE-404: Improper Resource Shutdown or Release

Description: The software fails to release or improperly releases a resource before it is made available for reallocation. In this case, deleting an object during traversal can lead to the rest of the traversal being aborted, potentially causing resource release issues.", "details": "Successful CWE mapping"}

{"cwe_mapping": "Based on the analysis provided, the most appropriate Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE) for the issue described is:

CWE-937: OWASP Top Ten 2013 Category A5 - Security Misconfiguration

Description: This weakness refers to insecure configurations that can lead to security issues within the application. In this case, the presence of "FIXME" indicates a known security issue that has not been resolved, potentially leaving the code vulnerable to exploitation.", "details": "Successful CWE mapping"}

{"cwe_mapping": "Based on the analysis provided, the most appropriate Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE) for the identified issue is:

CWE-398: Indicator of Poor Code Quality
Description: This weakness occurs when indicators of poor quality are present in a codebase, such as the use of "TODO" comments suggesting potential vulnerabilities or suboptimal implementations.", "details": "Successful CWE mapping"}

{"cwe_mapping": "Based on the analysis provided, the most appropriate Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE) for this self-admitted security debt related to code duplication would be:

